I sit in front of my computer.
My mother and my father speak.
Suddenly I hear a loud sound from the computer.
"Do I hear a dog?" I ask.
My father laughs.
"Yes, it is Lola!" he says.
He lifts a brown dog up in front of the camera.
She is my dog.
She has a small head and a black nose.
Lola looks directly into the screen.
She barks loudly.
I laugh and put my hand on my screen.
"Hello Lola," I say.
"Does she know my voice?" I ask.
"Yes, she knows your voice," my mother says.
I smile at my dog.
It is a lovely moment.
I miss my home, but I am happy now.
